    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class, the only one present). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table so the persisted value round-trips (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the GET response (MapStruct maps it automatically by name).\n\n4. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (new OfficeFloor function) \u2014 computes `LAST3` as the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and `NNNN` as `%04d` of `findAll().size() + 1` (\"one more than the current number of owners\"), then sets it on the entity in place.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignCustomerCode` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `ensureUniqueTelephone` and `save`, so the code is assigned before the owner is persisted.\n\nThe acceptance test's `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes: `smithers \u2192 SMI-\u2026`, `jones \u2192 JON-\u2026`, and the second owner's sequence is exactly one greater than the first (the first owner is committed and counted before the second is created).",
